course: dictionary
lesson: 2078
title: Big words from history and the news
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are built from a shorter word you may already know. A «constitution» is the set of main rules that says how a country is run. Add «-al» and you get constitutional, which means to do with that set of rules.
explain: «The King is head of state in a constitutional monarchy: he does not run the country or take sides.» Read the words around constitutional. A monarchy has a king or queen, and the rules limit what the king can do. So constitutional here means the king's powers follow the country's main rules.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning in. «The King and the royal family stay neutral: they do not vote and do not say which party they support.» Neutral means not taking sides, and that fits. Constitutional can also be an old-fashioned noun for a walk taken for your health, so the sentence clues tell you which meaning is right.
fact: Constitutional means to do with a country's constitution, its main set of laws about how it is governed and what rights people have.
fact: A law that is «constitutional» follows those rules, and an «unconstitutional» law breaks them.
fact: The USA has a written Constitution.
fact: In a «constitutional monarchy», the king or queen reigns but Parliament makes the laws. The UK, Australia and Canada are all constitutional monarchies.
fact: As a noun, «a constitutional» is an old-fashioned walk taken for your health.
exercise: The UK has a «constitutional monarchy». What does that mean? | A country where the king makes every law alone | A country with no laws at all | *A country where the king or queen reigns but Parliament makes the laws | A country with no king or queen
exercise: A law that breaks the country's main rules is called what? | *unconstitutional | constitutional | monarchy | constitution
exercise: In an old book, «a morning constitutional» means what? | *A walk taken for your health | A meeting with the king | A weakness in your body | A law about people's rights
test: The USA has a written what, which is its main set of laws? | *Constitution | Monarchy | Parliament | Crown
test: «A constitutional crisis» in the news is a serious problem about what? | A fight in a football match | *How the country's main rules and laws work | The weather forecast | Lost keys
exam: In «a constitutional weakness», what does constitutional mean? | To do with the country's laws | Very loud | *To do with a person's body or nature | Fast and clever
